winemac.drv: Export macdrv_functions for DXMT.

DXMT's winemetal.so creates its Metal layer through a table that it looks up
with dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, "macdrv_functions"), in the layout of CrossOver's
Wine. Stock Wine doesn't export it, and DXMT then fails with "Failed to create
metal view". Since Wine 10 the window data no longer has the client Cocoa view
DXMT reads, so get_win_data() here returns the old layout, backed by a client
surface made for the window and released when the window is destroyed.

Written for EscApp against Wine 11.0. Like the code it changes, this patch is
licensed under the GNU LGPL 2.1 or later (see the header of dxmt.c).

